      "status": "resolved",
      "finding": "The source documentation described the current Windows brain as an ONLOGON Scheduled Task.",
      "disposition": "Current behavior is documented as a per-user and per-channel HKCU Run value that starts a hidden PowerShell supervisor. The launcher writes an advisory supervisor/runtime PID record, and readiness is proven separately by an initialized runtime IPC response. Scheduled Tasks are legacy cleanup only.",
